ually responsible for  killing his son well  not bucky the winter soldier was bucky  killed him as the winter soldier when he  was under hydra's command  yori's name is on bucky's list in steve  rogers book that he has  he's been trying to make amends with him  but hasn't been able to summon the  courage to do it yet because it's a very  hard thing to tell him  but he's definitely going to do this in  the next episode and something peculiar  to note here  is how they talk about steve being gone  but notice how nobody ever says that  steve  died and even in the memorial museum for  captain america steve rogers they don't  say anything about him dying they just  said that he lived his life  so we really don't know what happened to  steve rogers at this point did he go  back to his own timeline or did he live  out sharon carter and stay in the main  timeline where he could have eventually  died  marvel can be pretty peculiar with their  words so i wouldn't be surprised if  steve actually went back to the old  timeline or if he's still alive  but they talk about how steve was their  connection to each other and now he's  gone so  now the two of them are friends now and  it's a great moment between the two of  them where bucky says that if you need  me  i'll be there for you and they actually  go from two people who  kind of hated each other to friends and  side note i was very wrong about this  being the final scene in the falcon in  the winter soldier and i'm glad i was  wrong because  i don't want to see them part ways i  hope they stick together even after the  series  now from here sam begins to prepare to  become captain america  throwing the shield in a way that peter  parker has described as defying the laws  of physics  and not obeying them at all he practices  throwing the shield and catching it  doing a bunch of maneuvers he runs  around the house telling his nephews  all day man a reference to steve rogers  catchphrase i can do this all day  we are literally 